2. COMMERCIAL LICENSE
------------------------------------------------------------

Any use of the Software that is not permitted under the Personal /
Non-Commercial License above requires a separate commercial license from
the copyright holder.

Examples of commercial use that require a commercial license include
(but are not limited to):

  - Embedding the Software, in whole or in part, in a paid product.
  - Operating the Software as part of a paid hosted service.
  - Deploying the Software inside a commercial organization for
    production purposes.

Business license per house. Deploying the Software inside a commercial
organization for its own use is licensed per house (one installation of
the Software with one agent) for a monthly or yearly fee. The license
covers the licensed houses for the time it is paid, including the updates
released in that time. The current price and what it includes are published
at https://embervy.ai/business.

Continuity. If the copyright holder publicly announces the end of
development, or publishes no release for twelve consecutive months, every
business license that was paid at that moment becomes perpetual and
irrevocable for the licensed houses and for all versions released until
then. No further fee is owed for them.

Evaluation. Trying the Software inside a commercial organization, one
house for up to 30 days, is not production use and needs no license.

Embedding the Software, in whole or in part, in a product of your own,
operating it as part of a paid hosted service, and more than ten houses
are licensed by separate agreement.

To obtain a commercial license, write to info@embervy.ai.


